+## Invoice notes, relations and merged amounts
+- `POST /invoices/<id>/notes` (form: `body`, optional `files` ×N) adds a note with optional attachments. Attachments use the same allowed types as invoice media.
+- `POST /invoices/<id>/links` (form: `linked_serial`, `link_type` = related | duplicate | adjustment, `amount_action` = none | merge, `link_note`) links two invoices in the same batch. `merge` appends the other invoice's total as one amount line on THIS invoice (Duplicate / Adjusted only). The other invoice is not changed.
+- `POST /invoices/<id>/links/<link_id>/delete` removes a link and reverses its merged line (refused if that line was edited since).
+- `GET /invoices/<id>/history` returns relations, merged amounts, notes and attachments from this invoice and every linked invoice the user may see (JSON).
+- Invoices with links cannot be deleted until unlinked. Visibility follows the invoice view (owner or administrator).
+- Tables: `invoice_notes`, `invoice_note_media`, `invoice_links`. Run `upgrade_database.py` offline on existing databases.
+
 ## Batch lifecycle additions
 Admin-only POST `/batches/<id>/lock`, `/unlock`, `/hide`, `/unhide`, `/archive`, `/unarchive`; GET `/batches/<id>/view`. Normal-user hidden-batch direct access returns 404; locked/archived mutations return permission errors. See `app/batches.py` and `BATCH-CONTROLS-UPGRADE.md`.
 
